  "note": "A2 liść · SECOND pack of the Oxford A2 vocab-gap build (VOCAB-BUILD-DIGEST batch 1). Grouping rationale: twelve Oxford-A2 building/place nouns taken as one theme, chosen because a1_places, a1_city and a2_travel have already built the frames these words need — prep_w_loc and prep_place have been live since A1, so the pack introduces ZERO structures. teaches_structures is [] by construction. A1/A2 already own dom, mieszkanie, sklep, szkoła, szpital, bank, poczta, apteka, hotel, restauracja, kawiarnia, kino, park, rynek, plac, most, dworzec, przystanek, lotnisko, muzeum-less list — those are ANCHORS here, never re-taught. Judgment calls, all reported: (1) TITLE. 'Miejsca 2' was the obvious match to a1_places ('Miejsca'), and was REJECTED: the plural miejsca is not in teaches_lemmas anywhere, only the singular miejsce, and a title may not carry an untaught form. 'W mieście' uses the taught locative phrase whole, on the a2_work2 ('W pracy') pattern. (2) TWO SENTENCES WERE REWRITTEN AFTER A POOL CHECK: 'To jest stare więzienie.' and 'Te schody są stare.' both failed because stare — the neuter singular and non-virile plural of stary — is NOT taught anywhere; the pool has stara/stary/starsza/starsze/starszy only. Rewritten to duże więzienie and schody są nowe, which use forms that are taught. The assumption that a paradigm is complete because its citation form is taught is exactly the trap the pool exists to catch. (3) SIX LOCATIVE FORMS are taught explicitly as whole w-/na- phrases, so every locative any sentence demands appears in a block and in teaches_lemmas (the every-form-taught rule), the same mechanism a2_house uses. kościół → w kościele carries the ó → o alternation and gets its own explain; it is a sound change inside one word, not a new system, and needs no structure ID. The remaining six nouns are used in the nominative only. (4) schody is plural-only, like meble in a2_house: it takes są, never jest, and no singular exists. (5) galeria is glossed 'gallery (for art)' deliberately — in everyday Polish it far more often means a shopping mall, and the gloss has to fence the sense the pack actually teaches. (6) Two emoji were rejected as visual anchors: 🚪 for brama (it reads as drzwi, already taught) and 🏠 for dach (it reads as dom). Where no safe icon exists the English gloss carries the anchor. (7) złodziej is recycled from a2_jobs2, the pack immediately before this one on the path — the first use of new vocab-gap material as an anchor for later vocab-gap material.",
